# ------------------------------------------------------------------- try

[break] try-fetches-the-corpus-for-every-test-run
rule: Only a run of the crates' perf tests fetches the corpus: a `test` run does not wait for it.
file: xtask/src/try_run.rs
in: reads_the_corpus
find: pair[1] == "perf"
replace: pair[1] != "zzz"
caught-by:
    try_run::tests::only_the_crates_perf_tests_fetch_the_corpus_of_real_code

[break] try-fetches-no-corpus-for-perf-tests
rule: `perf -p CRATE` fetches the corpus before it builds anything.
file: xtask/src/try_run.rs
in: reads_the_corpus
find: command.first().is_some_and(|verb| verb == "test")
replace: command.first().is_some_and(|verb| verb == "perf")
caught-by:
    try_run::tests::only_the_crates_perf_tests_fetch_the_corpus_of_real_code
